From: "JQE Chief Engineer (Claude)" <jqe-bot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 05:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/37] refactor: rewire main.py onto config/logging/exceptions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Uses config.settings instead of hardcoded literals (symbol,
  timeframe, candle count, balance, risk percent) — same default
  values, now overridable via environment/.env.
- Replaces print() with structured logging throughout.
- Raises typed exceptions (BrokerConnectionError, MarketDataError)
  instead of printing an error and returning early; disconnect() now
  runs in a finally block so it's always called.

Also fixes pre-existing dead imports discovered while wiring this up:
main.py imported 'get_candles' from core.market_data, 'generate_signal'
from strategy.signal_engine, 'evaluate_trade' from
risk.risk_controller, and an 'ExecutionSimulator' class from
execution.simulator — none of which exist anywhere in the codebase.
The real APIs (MarketData class, SignalEngine.generate(intelligence),
approve_trade(signal, market_data), simulate_trade(signal,
current_index, dataframe)) take fundamentally different arguments, so
wiring them correctly is a trading-logic integration decision, not a
Foundation-milestone one (see docs/architecture.md and the new
Milestone 2b in docs/roadmap.md).

main.py now stops after the last verified-real step (market data ->
validation -> indicators -> regime detection) and logs a clear warning
that downstream wiring is pending, instead of crashing on an
ImportError or fabricating an integration under time pressure.

Adds tests/test_main.py covering run()'s error paths and main()'s
top-level error handling.
